# BLE witness build options.
#
# Role is NOT here any more. It used to be a build-time choice, which meant a
# separate image per dongle and a reflash to move one from inside to outside.
# It is provisioned at install now and lives in settings.

mainmenu "ultrawidelock BLE witness"

config WITNESS_WINDOW_MS
	int "Summarisation window, milliseconds"
	default 2000
	range 250 10000
	help
	  How long each report covers. MEASURED 2026-08-11 on the previous
	  firmware: a filtered advertiser yielded 3-8 packets per 2000 ms
	  window, against the lock's minimum of 2 for a usable mean. Halving
	  this halves that count and starves the quorum; doubling it doubles
	  the time a walk-up needs to accumulate agreeing windows.

config WITNESS_PORT
	int "UDP port for reports and challenges"
	default 49180
	range 1024 65535
	help
	  Must match CONFIG_ULTRAWIDELOCK_WITNESS_PORT on the lock. Both ends
	  bind it: reports go up, the challenge nonce comes down.

config WITNESS_BOOT_TRACE
	bool "Light an LED at each boot milestone (BENCH ONLY)"
	default n
	help
	  The dongle has no debug connector, so firmware that dies before USB
	  enumerates cannot be diagnosed at all: no console, no RTT, nothing to
	  attach. This lights a different LED at PRE_KERNEL_1, POST_KERNEL,
	  APPLICATION and main(), and never clears them, so whatever is still lit
	  when the board stops says how far it got. See src/boot_trace.c.

	  Off in anything deployed: it takes the LEDs the status indication owns,
	  and two owners for one lamp is worse than no instrument.

source "Kconfig.zephyr"
